<title>FRANCE: Matra-Nortel unit seeks mobile phone partner.</title>
<headline>Matra-Nortel unit seeks mobile phone partner.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Matra Communication, a joint unit of Lagardere and Northern Telecom (Nortel), is looking for a partner in the business of mobile phone terminals, the newspaper Le Monde reported on Friday.</p>
<p>Citing union sources, it said Matra Communication would transfer its mobile phone network equipment manufacturing business to Nortel Matra Cellular (NMC), 17 percent owned by Matra Communication and 83 percent owned by Nortel, in January.</p>
<p>Matra officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
